{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3959","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3959","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3959\",\"parent_revision\":\"3323fd22d074fc33002434e46070115fa497e69841433049e8da70e0f917460c\",\"root_revision\":\"3323fd22d074fc33002434e46070115fa497e69841433049e8da70e0f917460c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Authorized Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe owner requested correction PRs for the outstanding cross-plugin review findings, and inline comments where an existing PR owns the affected behavior. Rechecked the open PRs in claude_skills and skill-lapidary before implementation. Related isolation, summarizer and instruction-audit stacks remain separate; none currently changes the affected contracts below.\\n\\nBaseline: claude_skills `37ab1028281c65eafc77741bb8f9832218488f9d`; methodology reference: skill-lapidary `408759274192a8e10e55445d1b8f173b588589ca`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Delivery Plan Acceptance Contract\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Evaluation integrity PR (review findings 1, 2, 3, 9): distinguish completed negative observations from errors/timeouts; isolate concurrent synthetic command files; do not label character counts as tokens or missing measurements as zero; derive observed repetition counts; align timing producers/consumers; keep incomplete evaluations out of successful optimizer completion/selection; identify the optimizer holdout as a selection set, not an untouched generalization test; reject duplicate query identity crossing partitions. Add discriminating offline tests and retain actual execution limitations.\\n- [ ] Goal authority PR (finding 4): user-approved intent and independently established repository authority outrank newly extracted descriptions of current behavior. Fresh extraction remains proposed until approved. Preserve material invariants/non-goals separately; report conflicts before pruning or overwriting approved goals. Keep the process lightweight and plugin-local.\\n- [ ] Process Siren PR (findings 5\u20138): separate task completion from process assessment; honor the caller's exact status envelope; detect repeated/no-progress candidate cycles separately from decomposition depth; make rendering subordinate to selected local resolution; do not label proposed/invalid/unvalidated representations authoritative by default; bind material-change evidence to source/candidate/contract/method identity and recheck before apply. Preserve ANALYZE/IMPROVE/REPRESENT, independent-work continuation and optional environment-neutral behavior sampling.\\n- [ ] Review final diffs and CI against the pinned revisions; publish evidence and missing verification, without claiming that authored behavioral scenarios were executed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Negative Controls Discriminating Cases\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAn unavailable LLM executable, timeout or malformed/unfinished stream must not pass a negative trigger case. Concurrent samples must not see another sample's synthetic command. Missing token/timing records must remain unknown, measured zero must survive, and a single observed repetition must not be reported as three. A fresh goal extraction conflicting with approved intent must not become pruning authority. Completed analysis of an invalid process may report successful task completion but must retain INVALID assessment. An A\u2192B\u2192A candidate loop must stop unresolved; a changed dependency must prevent stale evidence authorizing promotion. A low-risk parent node must remain concise while a consequential child is expanded.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Boundaries\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNo merge, approval, force push, unrelated cleanup, mandatory sampling tool, new multi-provider harness, database, or universal benchmark threshold. Process Siren sampling remains an optional methodology adapted by the executing agent to its environment. Existing provider-specific Skill Creator scripts are corrected, not imposed on Process Siren.\\n\\nRelated but not closed by this work: #3819 (full provider-safe behavioral runner), #3244 (diagram disclosure), #3492 (actual multi-harness certification), #544 (separate mission interview), #3946\u2013#3950 (plugin/pytest isolation stack), #3924\u2013#3927 (summarizer train), and skill-lapidary #195\u2013#197/#200.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Environment Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRepository reads/writes use the GitHub connector. Direct git network access in this sandbox failed DNS resolution; Claude/Codex executables are absent. Isolated deterministic tests may be run on byte-verified materialized fixtures. Full checkout, live LLM/host evaluation and fresh-agent verification must not be implied by those results.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"23cceec6531524f6768b9e3105ce13cf0222ce9ea1c4682fd2cb12ffaa1874a7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXOlR_Q\"}"}